.chapter
  h1 GROWTH AND DEVELOPMENT

  h2 Some Concepts Of Growth
  ol.complex-list
    li
      hl Concept of Normailty
    ul
      li Normal refers to which is usually expected / ordinary / typical.
      li Craniofacial growth changes with Age.
      li
        | Thus, what is normally seen in one age group 
        hl may be not be necessarily normal
        |  for different age group.
    li
      hl Rhythm of Growth
      | : According to Hooton
    p
      | Growth is not steady &amp; uniform, wherein all body parts enlarge at same rate, &amp; increment of 1 year equal to proceeding or succeding year.
    li
      hl GROWTH SPURTS
    p
      | Period when sudden acceleration of Growth. This sudden increase in growth, termed &apos;Growth Spurt&apos;
    p
      hl Cause of accentuated growth : 
      | Physiological alteration in hormonal secretion.
    h3 Timings Of Growth Spurts
    ol
      li Just before birth
      li 1 year after birth
      li
        hl Mixed Dentition growth spurt
      ul
        li
          hl Boys : 
          | 8 - 11 years
        li
          hl Girls : 
          | 7 - 9 years
      li
        hl Pre Pubertal growth spurt
      ul
        li
          hl Boys : 
          | 14 - 16 years
        li
          hl Girls : 
          | 11 - 13 years
    p
      hl &rarr; Growth modification by Myofunctional appliance
      |  gives better results during growth phase.
    p
      hl &rarr; Surgical Correction : 
      | done only after Cessation of Growth.
    li
      hl Differential Growth
      p
        | Human body doesn&apos;t grow at Same Rate Throughout Life. 
        br
        | Different organs grow at different rate, to different amount, at different times.
      ol
        li
          hl Scammon&apos;s Growth Curve
        li
          hl Cephalo caudal Gradient of Growth
    h3 Scammon&apos;s Growth Curve
    p Body tissues broadly classified into 4 types:
    .list-div
      ul
        li
          hl Lymphoid Tissues : 
          | grows rapidly in Late childhood &amp; reaches almost 200 % of adult size. 
          br
          | This is adaption to infection in children as they are more prone. 
          br
          | But, till 18 years age, it involutes to reach adult size.
        li
          hl Neural Tissue : 
          | Very rapidly &amp; reaches adult size by 6 - 7 years age. Very little growth occur after it. 
          br
          | This facilitates intake of further knowledge.
        li
          hl General Tissues or Visceral Tissues : 
          | Bone, Muscle &amp; other organs. 
          br
          | S- Shaped Curve : Rapid growth upto 2 - 3 years, 
          br
          | followed by Slow Phase between 3 - 10 years. 
          br
          | After 10th year Rapid Phase terminating by 18 - 20 years age.
        li
          hl Genital Tissues : 
          | Negligible growth until puberty, Rapid growth at puberty.
      img(src='../static/img/orthodontics/growth-development/scammonscurve.webp' alt="scammon's-curve")
    |  
    h3 Cephalo caudal Gradient of Growth
    p Axis of increasing growth extending from Head towards Feet.
    p
      | Post Natal growth is more in body parts away from 
      hl Hypophysis Cerebri.
    .list-div
      ol  
        li
          hl 3 Months I.U.L. :
          ul
            li Head = 50 %
            li Lower limbs = Rudimentry
        li    
          hl BIRTH :
          ul
            li Head = 30 %
        li    
          hl ADULT :
          ul
            li Head = 12 %
            li Lower limbs = 50 %
      img(src='../static/img/orthodontics/growth-development/cephalocaudal-body-gradient.jpg' alt="cephalocaudal-body-gradient")
      img(src='../static/img/orthodontics/growth-development/head-growth-gradient.jpeg' alt="head-growth-gradient")